From b5997ecafba00c8c8f2b7b2b4f7b3a86dabc8813 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 20:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Price single-tile sunk draft cost and halt dead DSpark Markov
 steps early

Upstream base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354
Rationale: At single-stream decode (c1, total_rows <= 16), DSpark executes its
block forward pass and sequential Markov draft loop before adaptive verification
scores the draft tokens, yet AdaptiveVerificationManager priced rows 2..6 at the
full-tile row slope (0.035) without the sunk drafting step cost (DRAFT_COST_RATIO)
or the within-16-row Tensor Core MMA tile marginal slope (SINGLE_TILE_ROW_COST_SCALE),
and OnlineAcceptanceEstimator started cold with zero intercepts until the first
IRLS refit. Conversely, at high concurrency (c8, c16) or when cumulative survival
already falls below effective_dead_rows_tau, executing all 5 sequential Markov
bias and vocabulary-parallel all_gather steps wastes per-step drafting latency on
unverified tail positions.
Quality implications: None (KL = 0); target rejection sampling verification is
unchanged and TP rank determinism is preserved.
Tests: pytest tests/v1/spec_decode/test_acceptance_estimator.py tests/v1/spec_decode/test_adaptive_verification.py tests/v1/worker/test_dspark_greedy_markov.py
Upstream status: Local patch for DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash DSpark speculative decoding.
